WEBVTT

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:05.230
<i>When a Chiba resident says they're going to Chiba Station,</i>

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.230
<i>you would unmistakably assume they were going to the station's east entrance.</i>

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.240
<i>But people from other prefectures might not be able to pick up on that.</i>

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.950
<i>It's sort of like when someone not from Tokyo says, "I'm going to Tokyo."</i>

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.750
<i>You get the feeling that they're off to chase their dreams and make it big.</i>

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.950
Sorry!

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.640
Hope you didn't wait. It took some time to get ready.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.260
You'd better believe I was waiting.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.500
Wouldn't the proper response be,
"Not at all, I just got here myself"?

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.890
We're headed out on a date, after all.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.060
A date?

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:50.440
Yes!

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.220
A theory to fill in the blanks

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.970
Ought to be the perfect fit

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.020
And yet it goes around in circles

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.310
The future is an unknown beast

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:27.150
All it takes is a crack

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.980
For it to be twisted

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.570
And stray from perfection

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.620
I'm walking down a path

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:44.290
That will eventually drain me of all warmth

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:49.460
If I want to change

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.250
It's now or never

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.300
I don't want an ideal replica

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:02.760
All I need is something real

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:08.650
I'll go look for it in the promised land

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.360
But you whisper to me

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.570
In a fairytale ending

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.910
The words I want to hear

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.580
Oh, it's Iroha!

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.230
Yo, 'sup!

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:32.140
Good afternoon! I'm glad you're still here.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.340
We were about to go home...

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.000
Did you have something to ask us?

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.550
Yes! That's right!

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.260
Do you have a moment?

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.640
Oh? Yeah...

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:44.900
I'll, uh..

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.440
Um, about the work I requested before...

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.770
Hm? Ah, I got it. I'll do something about it.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:00.890
Great! Then is tomorrow at ten in front of Chiba station all right?

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.110
What? Tomorrow?

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.370
Uh, I'm not sure I can...

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.140
But tomorrow's totally free, you know?

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:11.370
No, I don't know. You could tell me you're booked all morning, and I'd buy it.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.130
I meant <i>you're</i> totally free.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.510
Oh, you were talking about me.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:19.050
Wait, isn't it weird that you were talking about m–

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.400
I'll see you tomorrow, then.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:25.540
I'll be looking forward to seeing your plan in action!

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.640
A date?

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.880
Yes!

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.860
I'm pretty sure Hayama's about to be swamped with work.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:37.070
I thought casually introducing him to some light fun would be good.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.280
Huh. Makes sense.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.950
Isn't that why you said you'd think of a date plan?

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.770
Eh? Did someone say that? Who did? Me?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.210
Maybe I did.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.990
So? Where are we going?

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.230
You're just leaving it to the girl?

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:03.050
When I act alone I get excited while making intricate plans,

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.320
but when there's other people,
my style is to follow after them.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.830
Okay. Whatever.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.730
Let's think about it while walking around.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.740
It's cold out here.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:16.440
<i>And who do you think made me wait out here in the cold?</i>

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.470
Hey, what kind of places do you usually hang out in?

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.590
Home.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:22.590
Try again.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.120
O-Okay...

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.160
How about we just go to the movies for now?
We can kill two hours that way.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.050
When was it decided we're killing time?

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.190
Well, I guess I'll leave it up to you.

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.210
Then the movies it is.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.560
I want to watch this!

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.340
Then I'll watch this.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.720
We'll meet back here when we're done.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.070
Hmm? What?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.220
I see...

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.500
I guess I shouldn't have expected anything else.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.230
Bowling, billiards, and ping-pong, huh?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:03.350
Not like it matters for what we're doing,
but billiards doesn't exactly suit you.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:04.280
Leave me alone.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.540
Oh, but if it's ping-pong, you fit in!

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.120
I don't need your damage control.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.310
Let's play ping-pong instead of a movie!

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.870
Fine, but won't it be hard with those shoes?

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.610
W-What?

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:23.080
I just thought you're being surprisingly observant.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:27.670
I can tell that much even if I'm not being observant because you're taller than you normally are.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:38.700
Oh, it's true. You're closer than you are normally.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:51.090
Well, you can just borrow shoes.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:51.960
Yup!

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:56.520
<i>Jeez! How foxy is this girl?</i>

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:02.590
I haven't played ping-pong since classes in middle school!

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.660
You can choose it as an option for P.E when you're a second-year.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.480
All right!

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.640
So you'll treat me to lunch if I win?

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.190
That's fine, I guess.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:40.880
Die!

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.460
Uh, that last shout seemed a little out of place.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:49.220
<i>Why are you acting so triumphant with such a satisfied smile?</i>

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:52.350
All right, it's my serve.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:56.120
Oh! Wait a sec, wait!

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.470
Oh gosh, oh gosh...

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:58.320
Hyahh!

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.690
Nice try.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:18.830
<i>Keh! How unfair!</i>

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.170
<i>What's unfair, you may ask?</i>

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:26.550
<i>The table is completely getting in
the way. I can't see anything!</i>

