00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:04.960
What is this?

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.120
Is that oil? Maybe wax?

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.840
Let's eat.

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:39.700
It hurts to say it...

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.010
but it tasted good.

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:43.700
That's a relief.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:52.710
Well... I guess taking a girl into a shop that's hard to go alone to scores some points.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:56.050
Hungry for something sweet now?

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:57.720
Hm? Sure.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.050
<i>Hey, hey, seriously?</i>

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:04.470
<i>This is Chiba, you know. Is it okay for there to be a café like this?</i>

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.320
Then, let's g–

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:08.000
Crap.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.870
What? What is it?

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:16.050
It's the Vice President and Secretary.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:18.240
What? Are those two going out?

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:21.500
Who knows? I doubt it.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:25.370
Besides, it's a bit simplistic to say they're dating just from seeing them–

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.470
What was that? Were you hitting on me just now?

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:34.680
There's a limit to shamelessness, already acting like my boyfriend from just hanging out one time!

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:37.260
I'm sorry, but you can only do that after hanging out some more times!

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:41.330
Whatever, let's go inside. Outside is cold.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:44.010
Wait for me!

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:49.020
Well, that near-miss was honestly unexpected...

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:53.520
Next time let's go someplace where there's less people we know!

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.960
There's a next time?

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.990
Why do you seem kinda grumpy about that?

00:11:57.990 --> 00:11:59.820
Thank you for waiting!

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:03.530
Is this everything you ordered?

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.530
Oh, one sec!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.830
Can you take a picture of us?

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.750
Sure, no problem.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.600
Okay, make a peace sign! Peace!

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:17.870
No. It's not like I have to be in the photo.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.230
The ice cream's gonna melt.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.500
It won't melt that fast!

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.320
Come on, hurry up!

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:29.060
You should get just a bit closer.

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.190
Okay, here we go.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.000
Thank you so much!

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.300
<i>It did melt a bit after all...</i>

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:55.040
Well, I guess you scored ten points for today.

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.930
Ten out of what? Just curious.

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.960
Out of one hundred, of course!

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.050
Why that low?

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:05.850
Firstly, minus ten points because you weren't Hayama.

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:08.180
<i>This was an impossible challenge from the very start.</i>

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:12.950
Then, minus forty points if we include your conduct.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:15.140
That's, well... fair, I guess.

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.630
So you were at least a little self-aware...

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:23.450
It's minus fifty points for the part where you easily accepted a girl's invitation.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:24.610
Ow.

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.960
You're the one that called me out.

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.740
Plus, that's zero points.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:34.250
But I'll give you a bonus ten points because it was fun!

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.630
Thanks for that.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:41.380
How was it for you?

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:48.040
Well, it was along those lines for me too.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.260
It was a bit tiring, though.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.350
"Bit tiring"? Aren't you being a bit too frank?

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.270
That's fine though.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:59.270
It just means you were putting in that much effort as my partner!

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:04.470
What is with that <i>super</i> annoyed face?

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:07.410
There isn't a girl that isn't annoying.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:16.910
That's true. Well, it's more like there aren't any <i>people</i> who aren't annoying.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.960
Uwah, you're annoying!

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.910
<i>This girl is cruel!</i>

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.970
Today was a good enough reference, for now!

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:26.710
Thank you.

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.840
N-No problem.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.220
Make sure you properly learn from this reference as well!

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:36.170
Sure... I mean... what?

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:37.600
Thanks for today.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.790
I'll see you again at school.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.610
Be careful on your way back.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:49.490
<i>Girls are made of sugar, spice, and something nice.</i>

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.490
<i>I think that was from Mother Goose.</i>

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:57.500
<i>Though, I get the feeling Isshiki has a bit too much spice in her.</i>

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:02.500
<i>No matter how much sugar you mix in,
habaneros are still habaneros.</i>

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:06.160
<i>It won't be complete without something nice.</i>

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:10.640
Good work everyone!

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:14.310
Oh, Iroha! Yo, 'sup!

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:17.810
Thank you for your time the other day!

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:20.480
Yeah...

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:31.450
So, I was thinking...

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:34.830
What if the student council published a free brochure?

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.480
What?

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:45.590
The brochure'd be, like, this size, right?

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.670
Yes! Exactly like that!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.630
Sounds good. Though I don't know what you're going to make it about.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.970
I've sort of already decided on that.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:59.300
It'll have things like places to hang out, restaurants with good food, cute cafés...

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:00.930
I want to see that!

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:03.810
I don't really have any interest, so I don't have to see–

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.480
Oh my gosh! How cute!

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.730
It's great, isn't it?

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:09.920
Can you show me that photo just now again?

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:11.210
Yes, of course!

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:13.750
Th-Those cat sundries...

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:14.090
This is great too!

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:17.210
Can you print this out in the reference room afterwards?

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:15.650
This is super cute, too!

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.210
What else, what else?

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.370
Eh? What?

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.200
Ah... Yeah...

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:30.200
No, kinda... I-I'm thinking I'd like to try going there too...

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.940
It seems like a very fun photo, yes?

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:42.400
U-Um... I had him cooperate with me for the research...

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.310
Ah, that's right!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:47.400
Actually, all the pages haven't been filled yet so I was having trouble!

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.270
So...

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.010
Um... Then–

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:53.130
You'll do the coverage?

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:54.930
That's a life saver!

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:59.120
Ah, this is the student council's property, so feel free to use it!

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:02.380
Yukinon...

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:06.110
If it's on the weekend, I'm free.

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:13.120
Fine.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:22.260
<i>What kind of company slave am I to go out on my days of leisure two weeks in a row?</i>

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.810
Oh, you're early.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:31.680
It's normal conduct in society to arrive five minutes early.

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:33.490
Is that so?

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.820
Hikki! Yukinon!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:37.720
Yo, 'sup!

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.200
So, where are we going?

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:47.850
Yukinon, cute clothes like this definitely suit you!

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:50.370
D-Do they?

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:52.460
And things like this too!

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.530
That's definitely too...

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:58.600
What? It's fine, isn't it? It is! It really is! Try it on once!

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:58.600
Ah... Ah, no...

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:00.920
<i>Not good, not good.</i>

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:04.360
<i>When you're near stores like that,
your eyes get sucked right in.</i>

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:07.230
<i>It's just rude to stare. Yeah, total bad form.</i>

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:10.360
<i>But I'm gonna look anyway. I'm a guy, after all!</i>

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:15.010
You'll get reported if you conduct such suspicious activity.

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:17.440
I'm not going to get reported for <i>this</i>.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:20.640
At most, the shop assistant might come close and say something to me.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:23.500
That's already something you should try to avoid.

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:28.500
I just hope you can act in a way that doesn't embarrass us.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.380
Yeah. I'll be careful.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:48.970
Where's Yuigahama?

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:52.110
She's checking if we can use the store for the brochure.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:09.170
I wonder if Yuigahama's
negotiations have gone well...

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.490
<i>It's okay! There's still hope left!</i>

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.400
<i>If you think genetically, anyway.</i>

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.440
<i>Nope.</i>

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:35.400
<i>I know she's got that pesky, frisky love of cats,</i>

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:38.830
<i>but I wish she'd pay a little more attention to her surroundings.</i>

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:39.950
Look at this!

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.870
Hikki! Isn't this dog cute?

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.290
A miniature dachshund?

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:47.110
That's the same breed you're already raising.

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:51.250
Yup! I was wondering how she'd be as Sable's wife.

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:56.130
Here!

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:58.060
O-Okay...

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.180
I wonder if it's like this...?

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.390
What is?

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:08.070
N-Nothing!

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:12.310
<i>Oh, that's what...</i>

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:33.500
And then, it had been a while and we got on the monorail,

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.750
but we got lost on the way back home.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:38.270
Isn't a part of Chiba station in the middle of construction?

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:38.770
That's right.

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:41.260
Both the right and left became the East exit!

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:43.440
These are good!

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:45.010
All of them are just fine!

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:47.270
Really? That's a relief!

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:48.190
Yep!

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:55.770
I'm glad it seems to have become a proper reference.

00:20:58.330 --> 00:20:59.650
Oh, that's right!

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.120
It's a bit off to say "while we're at it",

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.530
but how about one photo of
everyone in the Volunteers Club?

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:08.730
Oh, good idea! Let's take one together too, Iroha!

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:11.200
Yes! Let's do it afterwards!

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.390
So, first let's take a photo of the Volunteers Club!

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:20.710
Yes, yes! That looks good!

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:22.800
Hey.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.910
Isn't this arrangement kind of weird?

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:27.370
Don't they kinda look like my paren–

00:21:26.190 --> 00:21:27.370
Hikigaya.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:28.960
You're being stubborn.

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:31.150
Iroha! We're all good!

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:32.810
Then I'm going to take it.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:35.230
Okay, say cheese!

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:40.920
Here you go.

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:43.110
It's a good photo, huh?

00:21:49.690 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>Indeed, it's not as bad as I thought.</i>

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:57.800
<i>I still don't know how to define or describe this club.</i>

00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:01.040
<i>But, if I put it in words, I felt that our feelings</i>

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:03.130
<i>were drawn in this photo.</i>

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:10.470
<i>That's why it's not as bad as I thought.</i>

00:22:26.770 --> 00:22:32.310
Be it our uniforms, or our textbooks

00:22:32.310 --> 00:22:37.800
They won't be changed on a whim

00:22:38.840 --> 00:22:44.750
These times are fun, if a bit hollow

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:50.780
We'll keep swimming through them

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:57.430
But to preserve this sense of calm

00:22:57.430 --> 00:23:02.980
We keep trying to solve the equation

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:06.520
Of the perfect act

00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:12.630
Solitude used to be our pillar of strength

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:18.670
But it started crumbling down once we found love

00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:24.900
Our everyday life could fall apart in a flash

00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:28.270
So we remain cowards

00:23:28.270 --> 00:23:31.130
As our overflowing emotions

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:37.370
Continue to hurt us forever
